From 8a097a829d5ec3af2458d8934dd1076e20f2507d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:59:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Document AccessDenied for a session that is not the
 caller's

This commit states in the interface description that a call that
names a session that does not exist, has closed or belongs to another
application fails with org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.AccessDenied, as in
the other portals that have sessions. The frontend already returns
that error; this adds the description.

Tested: the scenario checks pass 40 of 40 against the frontend.
---
 data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
index 13262f7..908d5c7 100644
--- a/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
+++ b/data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
       that the ``version`` property of this interface exists on
       org.freedesktop.portal.Desktop, and otherwise falls back to libsane.
 
+      A call that names a session that does not exist, has closed, or belongs
+      to another application fails with ``org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.AccessDenied``,
+      as in the other portals that have sessions.
+
       This documentation describes version 1 of this interface.
     -->
   <interface name="org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner">
